# Conditional Formatting & Highlight Measures

These measures return data only when specific conditions are met. They are used to highlight Highs, Lows, and Above/Below Average data points in the visualizations.

** Average Sales
dax:
Avg CY Sales = AVERAGEX(ALLSELECTED(Products[Product Name]), [CY Sales])

** Min / Max Identification

- Max Sales = MAXX(ALLSELECTED(Orders[Order Date].[Month]), [CY Sales])
- Min Sales = MINX(ALLSELECTED(Orders[Order Date].[Month]), [CY Sales])

- Min/Max Sales = 
VAR CurrentSales = [CY Sales]
VAR TotalSales = CALCULATE([CY Sales], ALLSELECTED(Orders[Order Date].[Month]))
VAR MaxSales = MAX(TotalSales, [CY Sales])
VAR MinSales = MIN(TotalSales, [CY Sales])
RETURN
    IF( CurrentSales = MaxSales || CurrentSales = MinSales, [CY Sales], BLANK() )

/* Note: 'Min/Max Profit' and 'Min/Max Quantity' use the same logic, 
   just replacing [CY Sales] with the respective metric. */


** Above / Below Average
- Sales - Above Avg = 
VAR CurrentSales = [CY Sales]
VAR AvgSales = [Avg CY Sales]
RETURN IF(CurrentSales >= AvgSales, CurrentSales, BLANK())

- Sales - Below Avg = 
VAR CurrentSales = [CY Sales]
VAR AvgSales = [Avg CY Sales]
RETURN IF(CurrentSales < AvgSales, CurrentSales, BLANK())


** Positive / Negative YoY
Positive YOY Profit = 
VAR Diff = [CY profit] - [PY profit]
RETURN IF( Diff > 0, Diff, BLANK() )

** Negative YOY Sales = 
VAR Diff = [CY Sales] - [PY Sales]
RETURN IF( Diff < 0, Diff, BLANK() )
